xvl (xv-light)

Overview

xvl is a minimalist image viewer built using only libX11 and stb_image libraries.
It supports displaying images with basic interactive controls and saving the displayed content.

Features

- Load and display images in formats supported by stb_image (JPEG, PNG, BMP, GIF).
- Load and display XBM, XPM, and XWD images.
- Zoom in and out using + and - keys (including numeric keypad).
- Pan the image with arrow keys.
- Mouse wheel zoom over the "[+/-]: Zoom" area.
- Mouse wheel vertical pan over the "[Arrows]: Pan" area.
- Left and right mouse clicks pan horizontally over the "[Arrows]: Pan" area.
- Save the currently displayed view as a PNG file by pressing s or clicking the save text.
- Quit the program by pressing q or clicking the quit text.
- Resizable window with smooth redraw and double buffering to minimize flicker.
- On-screen help text displaying controls.
- Window title dynamically shows the current image filename.
- Simple, dependency-light design, statically linkable for a small binary size.

Controls

Key         Action
---------------------------
+ / KP+     Zoom in
- / KP-     Zoom out
Arrow keys  Pan image
Mouse wheel over "[+/-]: Zoom"    Zoom in/out
Mouse wheel over "[Arrows]: Pan"  Pan up/down
Left click over "[Arrows]: Pan"   Pan left
Right click over "[Arrows]: Pan"  Pan right
s           Save current view to output.png
q / Esc     Quit program

Usage

./viewer <imagefile>

Example:

./viewer test.png
